        An IRS <strong class="cp504-gold">CP504 notice</strong> is a formal Notice of Intent to Levy. It means the IRS is preparing to <strong class="cp504-gold">seize your state tax refund</strong> to satisfy unpaid taxes. The notice says that if you do not pay or arrange payment within <strong class="cp504-gold">30 days of the notice date</strong>, the IRS can levy your state tax refund. CP504 alone does not let the IRS take wages or bank funds: that needs a later final notice (LT11 or Letter 1058).
      </p>
    </div>
