      <li>
        <strong>Step 1 — Identify Your 30-Day Deadline.</strong> Look at the Notice Date at the top right of your CP504 letter. Add 30 calendar days — this is your absolute deadline to prevent state refund seizure.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Step 2 — Set Up an Online Payment Plan Immediately.</strong> Go to <a href="https://www.irs.gov/payments/online-payment-agreement-application" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">irs.gov/opa</a> and apply for an Installment Agreement. Once approved online, active levy procedures on CP504 are automatically suspended.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Step 3 — Request Hardship Status if Unable to Pay.</strong> If you cannot afford monthly payments, call the IRS at 1-800-829-1040 to request Currently Not Collectible (CNC) status based on necessary living expenses.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Step 4 — Ask for an appeal if you disagree.</strong> If you disagree with the collection action, the notice explains how to request an appeal under the Collection Appeals Program (Form 9423) within 30 days of the notice date.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <div class="cp504-pro-tip">
